\paragraph{Iteration and cognitive models of writing.}
Iterative generation methods improve text through repeated feedback and revision~\citep{madaan2023self,du2022iterative}, and PEER~\citep{schick2023peer} trains a model to imitate the writing process by proposing and explaining edits, while cognitive writing research offers a process-level account of how planning, drafting, and reviewing interact~\citep{flower1981cognitive,hayes1996new,hayes2012modeling}.
\citet{gero2022design} use those processes to organize writing-support systems, and CogWriter~\citep{wan2025cognitive} likewise draws on cognitive writing theory to structure planning, generation, and revision.

replacements.before:
\paragraph{Alternative writing systems.}
We compare three alternatives to \condAgenticCogWriter: (1) \condSinglePass\ produces the complete document in one generation call; (2) \condStaged\ executes \texttt{Pre-Write}$\rightarrow$\texttt{Write}$\rightarrow$\texttt{Re-Write}, following the common separation of planning, drafting, and revision~\citep{yang2022re3,wan2025cognitive}; and (3) \condTaskPlanning\ follows a WriteHERE-style adaptive task graph~\citep{xiong2025beyond}, recursively decomposing the assignment and selecting among dependency-satisfied task nodes.
The alternatives therefore advance a whole document, a fixed writing stage, or an adaptive task node, whereas our system advances a writing process.

replacements.after:
\paragraph{Alternative writing systems.}
We compare three alternatives to \condAgenticCogWriter: (1) \condSinglePass\ produces the complete document in one generation call; (2) \condStaged\ executes the \texttt{Pre-Write}$\rightarrow$\texttt{Write}$\rightarrow$\texttt{Re-Write} stage model~\citep{rohman1965pre}, with which \citet{flower1981cognitive} contrast their process model; and (3) \condTaskPlanning\ follows a WriteHERE-style adaptive task graph~\citep{xiong2025beyond}, recursively decomposing the assignment and selecting among dependency-satisfied task nodes.
The alternatives therefore advance a whole document, a fixed writing stage, or an adaptive task node, whereas our system advances a writing process.

